It's also important to note, that PexAssertions should be used in the context of a unit test method (like a test method in a test class annotated with `[Test]` or a method marked with `[TestMethod]` attributes) and they do not automatically get converted to `Debug.Assert` in the generated test methods. Debug.Assert are used in certain scenarios for runtime checks. There are scenarios where Pex generates assertion checks for you but in general, this is used alongside Assert, when we want to test conditions which should be true but Pex can't capture.

